,{"type":"text","text":"exists (NetworkX "},{"code":"minimum_weight_full_matching","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"): scipy’s assignment on the biadjacency"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"matrix, rows ","type":"text"},{"code":"bipartition.left","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", columns ","type":"text"},{"code":"bipartition.right","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in these orders (NetworkX’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"columns follow set iteration, so its matching can differ among equal-weight ones), missing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"edges forbidden, each pair’s lightest copy (NetworkX keeps the last copy on a multigraph). The matrix is never built: memory O(n + m). An empty","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"side gives the empty matching. ","type":"text"},{"code":"weight","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is called once per edge, in position order.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"O(s² t), s ≤ t the side sizes.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/matchingmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumweightfullmatching(bipartition:weight:)","role":"symbol"},"doc://MatchingModule/documentation/MatchingModule/GraphProtocols/Graph/maximumMatching()":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MatchingModule\/documentation\/MatchingModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/maximumMatching()","title":"maximumMatching()","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maximumMatching","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Matching","preciseIdentifier":"s:14MatchingModule0A0V","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A maximum-cardinality matching by Edmonds’ blossom algorithm: for each still-free vertex in"},{"type":"text","t